  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Read through the Agda formalization accompanying
<fr:link href="/alexandruIntrinsicallyCorrectAlgorithms2025-preprint/" title="Intrinsically Correct Algorithms and Recursive Coalgebras" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/alexandruIntrinsicallyCorrectAlgorithms2025-preprint/" display-uri="alexandruIntrinsicallyCorrectAlgorithms2025-preprint" type="local">[alexandruIntrinsicallyCorrectAlgorithms2025-preprint]</fr:link>, hosted at
<fr:link href="https://git8.cs.fau.de/software/intrinsically-recursive" type="external">git8.cs.fau.de/software/intrinsically-recursive</fr:link>.</html:p>
    <html:p>Focus on how recursive coalgebras are defined and what type-theoretic
machinery (sized types, guarded recursion, well-founded recursion) is used to
enforce termination.</html:p>
